<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:13:25 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel votes in first election since October 7 attack as Netanyahu faces crucial test</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-2026-netanyahu-october-7</link><description>
Israelis head to the polls on Tuesday for the first time since Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack, in a closely contested election seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. The vote follows three years of regional wars, with Netanyahu running neck and neck with centrist rival Gadi Eisenkot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38436e56-cf0c-11f1-af1b-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-22T214048Z-992217913-RC2L8OAE7RTT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-NETANYAHU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38436e56-cf0c-11f1-af1b-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-22T214048Z-992217913-RC2L8OAE7RTT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-NETANYAHU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3489a87a-d1b9-11f1-a049-cdfa7776efb6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:12:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38436e56-cf0c-11f1-af1b-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-22T214048Z-992217913-RC2L8OAE7RTT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-NETANYAHU.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Mecca pact nations hold talks with Iran to prevent renewed Middle East war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-iran-talks-mecca-pact-nations-war</link><description>
Senior officials from Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan held talks in Iran on Monday aimed at preventing renewed fighting in the Middle East, with Tehran describing discussions as “very good”. The diplomatic push, attended by Saudi Defence Minister Prince Khalid bin Salman, followed warnings from Washington, Tehran and Israel of renewed hostilities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/484996fa-cd8f-11f1-8da3-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2f310afab0f2ee355e67e96c836f9f342820c590.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/484996fa-cd8f-11f1-8da3-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2f310afab0f2ee355e67e96c836f9f342820c590.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2221de74-d190-11f1-b36d-433050913ecb</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:24:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/484996fa-cd8f-11f1-8da3-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2f310afab0f2ee355e67e96c836f9f342820c590.jpg">© Fayez Nureldine, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>UN cites 'ethnic cleansing' concerns around Israel's Palestinian displacement operation in Hebron</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron</link><description>
The United Nations on Monday raised "ethnic cleansing" concerns following Israel's operation to displace by force more than 3,000 Palestinians from their homes in Hebron in the West Bank after two Palestinian gunmen killed two Israeli soldiers at a checkpoint near the city on Friday. UN rights chief Volker Turk said in a statement that the "aggressive operation" must end, and that "collective punishment is a grave violation of international law".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f768b06-d163-11f1-8123-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26297362966211.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f768b06-d163-11f1-8123-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26297362966211.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73cbd45c-d161-11f1-9951-9f18de484212</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:59:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f768b06-d163-11f1-8123-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26297362966211.jpg">© Mahmoud Illean, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Opponents accuse Netanyahu of stoking tensions with Iran before Israel's election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election</link><description>
Israel's defence minister denied on Monday (October 26) reports of a rift between PM Netanyahu and the army over Iran, before the vote.  Netanyahu has campaigned heavily on his security credentials, insisting only he can "finish the job" in the US-Israeli war on Iran. His main rival, ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot, has accused him of playing up the Iran threat when it suits him politically, and of failing to accomplish his war goals. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e69e600-d15c-11f1-948d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-170817-171420-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e69e600-d15c-11f1-948d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-170817-171420-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93b3e43a-d15c-11f1-93a3-1f00e589717b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:11:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli candidate Eisenkot pledges to unite country as Netanyahu deems him 'soft' on Iran</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran</link><description>
Israeli presidential candidate Gadi Eisenkot's pledge made Sunday to "heal" Israeli society after Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's divisive tenure resonated with some voters attending his final campaign rally before polling begins Tuesday. Netanyahu meanwhile received fresh backing for re-election from US President Donald Trump and deemed Eisenkot "soft" on Iran. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d413bfb8-d158-11f1-ac33-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3UD2UE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d413bfb8-d158-11f1-ac33-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3UD2UE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3256e2c0-d155-11f1-bf54-0f48f32af499</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:58:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d413bfb8-d158-11f1-ac33-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3UD2UE.jpg">© Jack Guez, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel election: unable to vote from abroad, expats have to fly home</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home</link><description>
Israelis can’t vote from abroad, so tens of thousands of expats are expected to fly home for the election. At Tel Aviv airport, supporters of opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot are already waiting at arrivals. A “Fly and Vote” initiative helps expats organise their trip, despite a failed petition from Netanyahu’s Likud party to restrict it. With polls predicting a tight race, every vote could count, and the result will decide the Prime Minister’s fate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/174cfc2a-d15b-11f1-8429-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-EN-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/174cfc2a-d15b-11f1-8429-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-EN-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82e24e68-d15b-11f1-93e5-f391c4eb952e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:47:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Jordan's strikes on Syria over church terror attack kill several civilians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church</link><description>
Jordanian authorities on Monday arrested three suspects over last week's terror attack that killed nine people in a church funeral procession in the village of Hammoud. Jordan's military later launched strikes on "terrorist organisations" in neighbouring Syria in retaliation for the attack by alleged Islamic extremists, killing at least eight civilians including women and children, a health official said. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94116308-d06c-11f1-88fd-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/b65b319e54017e17feaa4f11998604f254a999a2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94116308-d06c-11f1-88fd-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/b65b319e54017e17feaa4f11998604f254a999a2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2ded65f4-d14d-11f1-acd0-7d88c33f0f1f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:12:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94116308-d06c-11f1-88fd-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/b65b319e54017e17feaa4f11998604f254a999a2.jpg">© Ahmad Shoura, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tens of thousands of Israelis living abroad expected to fly in for pivotal vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote</link><description>
Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27). Unable to vote from abroad, tens of thousands of expatriate citizens have been flying in from across the world to cast their ballots. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky met some of them at the airport.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fc43c96-d142-11f1-abf3-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140748-141044-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fc43c96-d142-11f1-abf3-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140748-141044-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84c0d38a-d142-11f1-9756-ef57fd2daebf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:20:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will Netanyahu's security promise win him this election?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election</link><description>
Since the beginning of his political career, Benjamin Netanyahu, Israel's longest-serving prime minister, has campaigned on a promise that he is the only one who will keep the Jewish state safe. As Israelis head to the polls for their first election since the October7 Hamas attacks and the start of the war in Gaza, Netanyahu's strategy might be less effective. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08eb65f0-ceb2-11f1-8538-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/Netanyahu-cover.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08eb65f0-ceb2-11f1-8538-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/Netanyahu-cover.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb6951b2-ceb0-11f1-b514-15a2577825cb</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:52:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel braces for national elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu</link><description>
Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27)  in the first elections since the October 7th attacks in 2023. Unable to vote abroad, expatriate citizens have been flying in from around the world to participate in a vote widely seen as being a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0337c57c-d128-11f1-bdd9-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090953-091147-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0337c57c-d128-11f1-bdd9-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090953-091147-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d77b164-d128-11f1-8057-4f90e64047c9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:35:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Arab Israeli voters could prove decisive in the upcoming elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections</link><description>
In Israel’s election the vote of Arab Israeli citizens could be crucial for the outcome and fate of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu who is standing for re-election. Traditionally voting turnout is lower among Arab Israelis than among the rest of the population. But this time some feel it’s their duty more than ever to cast their ballot given the policies and wars undertaken by Netanyahu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a94a6d8-d12a-11f1-83a6-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-091218-091500-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a94a6d8-d12a-11f1-83a6-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-091218-091500-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f922ee4-d12a-11f1-9536-e32dde40c127</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:13:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>A look at the main issues in Israeli elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu</link><description>
Israelis will vote Tuesday (October 27) in the first national elections since Hamas' Oct. 7, 2023, attack in what is widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership. He rejected ICC war crimes claims and denied corruption as national elections approach. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be013ffa-bc7e-11f1-adb1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25357403714237.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be013ffa-bc7e-11f1-adb1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25357403714237.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef307628-d131-11f1-9213-6ff749a9a215</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:59:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Israeli election seen as a referendum: For or against Netanyahu?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has led his country almost continuously for nearly 17 years. But will he manage to retain power following Tuesday's election? Netanyahu's latest term has divided Israeli society more than ever and will be marked by the October 7 attacks, his handling of the conflicts in Gaza, Iran and Lebanon, as well as his controversial judicial reform. FRANCE 24's David Gilberg reports, with Lauren Bain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0152e22a-cf05-11f1-a645-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ISRAEL-ELEX-BIBI-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0152e22a-cf05-11f1-a645-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ISRAEL-ELEX-BIBI-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3f13af90-cf05-11f1-b3ea-bb3c152805dc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:40:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>David GILBERG</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Report: IDF chief pushes back on Netanyahu's order</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261025-report-idf-pushes-back-on-netanyahu-s-order</link><description>
An extraordinary confrontation at the top of Israel's leadership, just two days before the election. Israeli media report Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and military chief Eyal Zamir are at odds over Iran. Zamir reportedly fears government instructions could trigger an immediate military escalation and has demanded written authorisation. Netanyahu denies any confrontation. The reports come as he warns Iran could attack Israel to disrupt Tuesday's vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4aad600-cf12-11f1-864d-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-56236f89.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4aad600-cf12-11f1-864d-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-56236f89.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14d89292-d0c5-11f1-9d88-77705c6fef84</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:24:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Demonstrators rally against government ahead of election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election</link><description>
In Israel, the anti-Netanyahu movement is mobilising. Thousands gathered in Tel Aviv on Friday to protest against the Israeli government, just three days ahead of a general election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4abc8a7a-d067-11f1-a9cf-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110931-111122-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4abc8a7a-d067-11f1-a9cf-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110931-111122-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fa70b32-d067-11f1-84c1-4f61f4eb9a12</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:38:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank: Families forcibly displaced in Hebron</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron</link><description>
More Palestinian families have been displaced in the occupied West Bank as Israeli forces continue operations in Hebron, following a deadly shooting that killed two Israeli soldiers on Friday. With elections scheduled for Tuesday, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has vowed a heavy response to the attack. Morgaene Ayre has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/11d151aa-d067-11f1-9d2a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110725-110909-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/11d151aa-d067-11f1-9d2a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110725-110909-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16e4f84a-d067-11f1-bf8e-31e55578324b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:35:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Thousands take to Tel Aviv's streets for protests against Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu</link><description>
Thousands marched against Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government in Tel Aviv on Saturday – just three days before Israel's general election – demanding accountability for the failure to prevent a Hamas-led attack on October 7, 2023, which led to the war in Gaza.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/234bdf36-cfd6-11f1-80cc-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4BH8JA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/234bdf36-cfd6-11f1-80cc-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4BH8JA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">930c3626-cfd2-11f1-8b5f-e72073f9c894</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:21:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/234bdf36-cfd6-11f1-80cc-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4BH8JA.jpg">© Jack Guez, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthi rebels claim new attacks on oil facilities and airports across Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia</link><description>
Yemen’s Iran-allied Houthi rebels said they launched attacks at Saudi oil facilities and airports on Saturday while Yemen’s Saudi-backed government ​said the ‌group also fired three ballistic missiles at coast guard sites in ⁠the port city of Aden.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1192dd1a-cfd3-11f1-97a7-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/King-Khalid-International-Airport.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1192dd1a-cfd3-11f1-97a7-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/King-Khalid-International-Airport.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64809fd0-cfd3-11f1-b5b8-8f1753211f55</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:50:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1192dd1a-cfd3-11f1-97a7-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/King-Khalid-International-Airport.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel begins demolitions in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-begins-demolitions-in-west-bank</link><description>
The Palestinian Authority has called for international pressure on Israel after a Palestinian official said around 1,200 Palestinians in Hebron in the West Bank were forced to leave their homes following an attack on Friday which killed two Israeli soldiers. The head of Hebron's municipality said an additional 1,300 may also be forced to leave.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6d1d9fc-cfbe-11f1-b89b-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-161247-161339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6d1d9fc-cfbe-11f1-b89b-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-161247-161339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc10e1c4-cfbe-11f1-bc2f-d5fd7e8fb465</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:13:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel to close all West Bank land crossings on election day</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israel-to-close-all-land-crossings-with-west-bank-on-election-day</link><description>
